You are going to redesign the information architecture of my existing engineering portfolio.

IMPORTANT:

This is NOT a visual redesign from scratch.

The current portfolio already has a distinctive cyber / terminal / system HUD / orbital control-plane aesthetic. Preserve that design language.

Do NOT convert the site into a generic developer portfolio with a white background, profile photo, About Me / Skills / Projects template.

The goal is to improve recruiter readability, engineering evidence density, and information architecture while preserving the existing identity.

==================================================
1. PRIMARY GOAL
==================================================

The current homepage behaves too much like a portal:

Hero
→ "Choose your next area"
→ Career
→ Engineering Projects
→ Certification Vault
→ Engineering Lab

This forces recruiters to click multiple pages before understanding the candidate.

Redesign the homepage into a SINGLE-PAGE ENGINEERING OVERVIEW.

A recruiter should understand the candidate's engineering profile within approximately 30–60 seconds without leaving the homepage.

Deep-dive pages should still exist.

The new model is:

Homepage
    ↓
Understand the engineer

Deep-dive pages
    ↓
Explore detailed evidence

The guiding principle is:

"Show the evidence first. Exploration comes second."

